  "id": 73284631,
  "iid": 506,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "STUN: add an option to auto-detect STUN protocol version",
  "description": "Commit 3a5d0569d7 added support for different STUN protocol versions; a global preference allows the user to select the desired flavour.\n\nUnfortunately, it is pretty common to have different flavours in the same capture file, or even in the same packet (with STUN messages encapsulated in a TURN tunnel), so a global preference applied to the entire file might not provide enough flexibility.\n\nAdd a basic auto-detect algorithm to identify the STUN version specific to each STUN message (the users will still have the option to force a global version)\n\nThe attached pcap ([msteams_android_app_videocall_from_calling_side.pcapng](/uploads/a4234355f09b0004170599f2aa2d1890/msteams_android_app_videocall_from_calling_side.pcapng)) has been captured while making a video call from MSTEAMS app.\nYou can notice that, for example:\n* flow \"udp.stream eq 88\" should be decoded as RFC5389; if you decode it as MS-TURN all \"Binding Request\" messages are wrongly dissected\n* flow \"udp.stream eq 75\" should be decoded as MS-TURN\n* in the flow \"udp.stream eq 77\" STUN messages are encapsulated (via DATA attribute) in other STUN messages. Inner messages should be decoded as RFC5389, while the outer ones as MS-TURN.\n\nNote that this algorithm doesn't handle the NET_VER_3489 version.\n\nAs for the latter, I am a bit confused about it and why it has been added in the first place. RFC3489 traffic seems to be handled by packet-classicstun.c dissector and not by packet-stun.c dissector: the latter always checks for the message cookie tag which doesn't exist in RFC3489 packets. In other words, AFAIU the STUN dissector will never be triggered by RFC3489 flows. What am I missing?",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2020-10-05T17:45:27.273Z",
  "updated_at": "2020-10-06T14:11:48.429Z",
